 "summary": "Only on 1h and daily, and only on the long side. After the squeeze fired with positive momentum, price moved more than after random candles on 1h and daily, but those entries cluster in volatile candles in a window that rose, and on daily the result came from uptrends only. Momentum crossing up zero did the same as random on all three timeframes, and leaving a squeeze with rising momentum beat random only on 1h, on one stretch.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Squeeze fires with positive momentum",
   "verdict": "edge",
   "text": "Beat random on 1h and daily, and the same as random on 4h. These candles are volatile ones in a window that rose, so price moved more after them; it is not a call on direction."
  },
  {
   "use": "Momentum crosses up zero",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily across the three pairs. Only SOL on 1h beat random on its own."
  },
  {
   "use": "Out of a squeeze with rising momentum",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "Beat random on 1h only because of signals on Nov 4–7, 2020, and without them it was the same as random. These are volatile candles in a window that rose, and on 4h and daily the result was the same as random."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, the squeeze firing with positive momentum gave 2,644 entries in 2,172 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.15% ahead of random entries, just above the luck band's top of 0.13%. The result holds without its strongest stretch and at 10 candles, but not at 50 or 100. The squeeze fires in volatile candles in a window that rose, so price moved more after them, which is not the same as picking direction.",
  "Split by coin or by trend, the 1h result thins out. On BTC it rests on signals on Mar 12, 2023, and on ETH on signals on Aug 18–19, 2026, while SOL did the same as random. In uptrends it rests on signals on Jan 2–3, 2021, and in downtrends it did the same as random.",
  "On daily, the same setting gave 100 entries in 90 moves and was 6.07% ahead of random after 20 days, above a band that tops out at 4.35%. It holds without its strongest signal, on Feb 3, 2021, and at 10 days, but not at 50 or 100. In uptrends it was 6.76% ahead, and in downtrends it did the same as random. On 4h it was only 0.02% ahead, inside the band.",
  "Momentum crossing up through zero did the same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. On SOL alone it beat random by 0.21% on 1h, held without its strongest signal and showed at 10 candles, but not at 50 or 100. On 4h, ETH was 0.68% ahead at 20 candles only. On 4h in downtrends it was 0.46% ahead, and that rests on signals between Aug 13, 2026 and Aug 17, 2026.",
  "Out of a squeeze with rising momentum enters on every candle the condition holds, so many of its entries sit inside the same move. Its 0.08% lead on 1h rests on 53 entries on Nov 4–7, 2020, the days after the US presidential election, and without them it did the same as random. On daily, SOL's 6.8% lead comes from 39 entries between Jul 22, 2021 and Sep 10, 2021, in a window that rose, so it reflects when the signal fired rather than which way price went.",
  "For a long DCA bot, the squeeze firing with positive momentum is the one setting after which price moved more than after random candles, and that faded by 50 candles. That shape fits a take profit reached within 10 to 20 candles better than a deal left open on deep DCA orders. On daily the result came from uptrends, so test it as a filter alongside a trend condition, not as an entry on its own. Leave the zero cross out as a reason to enter, since it did the same as random."
 ],
